    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.28) headlining our offensive attack. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** represents our strongest play, bolstered by a juicy matchup against Pecko, whose 5.95 xERA is the most exploitable arm on the board; the combination of a favorable park factor and a +14% dynamic platoon advantage makes him an elite start in the MI slot. **Kyle Tucker** remains a pillar of consistency, facing the mid-tier Elder with enough SP skill margin to maintain his high floor, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.26) also provides significant upside in the UTIL spot, as his positive park and matchup metrics outweigh a minor platoon drag.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision occurred at the BN spot, where **Miguel Vargas** finished at a 39.60 efficiency score, narrowly missing the 40.0 baseline required to unseat our lower-tier starters. While his xwOBA remains strong at 0.389, the combination of facing a dominant arm like deGrom and the negative impact of his \"Elite Hold\" status\u2014which heavily penalizes his limited stolen base utility\u2014kept him on the pine. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Nasim Nunez** (41.15) and **Sam Antonacci** (46.73); while both are active, they are essentially fading against elite pitching talent today. **Nasim Nunez**\u2019s score is particularly suppressed by his batting order slot, though his speed remains a necessary risk in our hunt for stolen bases.\n\nWe are monitoring several high-risk matchups today where elite pitching threatens to stifle our production. **Jackson Merrill** (48.97) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (50.56) both draw daunting assignments against Skenes and Harrison, respectively. While **Luis Robert Jr.** retains a healthy platoon edge, the \"Elite Hold\" penalty associated with his matchup limits his ceiling. Furthermore, we remain without key depth pieces **Jordan Westburg**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson** due to injury, leaving us with little room for error if weather or late lineup scratches materialize. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** are locked in despite challenging matchups against Liberatore, as their base projection levels are high enough to justify the start even when facing a tough southpaw.",
